# nisse sudo mode LIMITED. Only the nisse snapshot helper and the read-only snapshot list are passwordless (the helper checks
# its own arguments; the list changes nothing). Every other sudo needs the wheel user's password: a terminal asks on the
# terminal, and sudo run by an AI session (no terminal) opens a password popup through the nisse sudo shim. That includes
# the rollback itself: the panel's undo button asks for the password in the same popup. One answer is remembered for a few
# minutes for every caller with no terminal, so a session that needs several commands is asked once. Switch with:
# sudo nisse-sudo-mode full
Defaults:%wheel timestamp_type=global
%wheel ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/nisse/nisse-snapshot-batch
%wheel ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/nisse-rollback list
